                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "282a8365-2235-3ce5-a8f0-4b0097de30e4",
                        "entry_id": "db8341b9-3a4a-335e-a38e-7295d911c027",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Fantasmer qu’on possède une caractéristique qu’on a vue quelque part."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e25cef91-032b-4b07-a396-106243c6aaed",
                        "source_entry_id": "db8341b9-3a4a-335e-a38e-7295d911c027",
                        "source_sense_id": "282a8365-2235-3ce5-a8f0-4b0097de30e4",
                        "target_lang_word": "introject",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "introject",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ea106429-c788-37d9-b62b-3c1b4d5058c9",
                                        "entry_id": "6361a8f5-da40-3b88-9dc8-a0fe7acbf0d9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To unconsciously incorporate into one's psyche."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2e166ed1-dab2-4961-b0aa-a19e66b211e1",
                                                "sense_id": "ea106429-c788-37d9-b62b-3c1b4d5058c9",
                                                "text": "Sometimes the attempt was made to reduce the inner to the outer world (Condillac, Mach, Avenarius, materialism); sometimes the outer to the inner world (Descartes, Berkeley, Fichte); sometimes the sphere of the absolute to the others (e.g., by trying to infer causally the essence and existence of something divine in general); […]; sometimes the general differentiation of subject and object to pregivenness of the co- or 'fellow-man', to whom an environmental element—as, for instance, 'this tree' — is supposed to be introjected, followed by subsequent introjection by the observer to himself (Avenarius); sometimes one's own body to a merely associative coordination of the self-perception of the own self and organ sensations with the own body as perceived from outside."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "introject",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1d6c024a-30e9-3f8f-b4b2-fc2781d707b0",
                                        "entry_id": "959aa417-b02c-304e-9699-5347164ac8d2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An element of another person that is unconsciously incorporated into one's psyche."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "15e703a9-c23a-4d61-be85-478f41fc6182",
                                                "sense_id": "1d6c024a-30e9-3f8f-b4b2-fc2781d707b0",
                                                "text": "When introjects are weak (or even absent), an anaclitic personality configuration results, characterized by dependency, insecurity, and feelings of helplessness and emptiness."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "14aefd99-9921-4cea-9ead-d6a6a7e18a57",
                                                "sense_id": "1d6c024a-30e9-3f8f-b4b2-fc2781d707b0",
                                                "text": "Repetitious comments are other examples of introjects that we take on as if they were truths. These include: You're lazy; you're selfish; you'll never amount to anything; […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
